Z||000001||WKDFIRO||06-02-2001||09:47 PM||||Ya killin' us!<P>What year? What engine? Is it a Fiero? Is it a GT? Is it Honda Prelude?<P>What!!!!<P>Seriously, have you already done a tune up? Usually if its a Fiero, the replacement of the pick up coil and module as a part of a very complete tune up will usually make a difference! <P>If you have already done that you might want to clean up the IAC valve. Sometimes a chunk of carbon can gum it up.<P> <p>[This message has been edited by WKDFIRO (edited 06-02-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000002||c m west||06-02-2001||11:29 PM||||Ok.....<P> 1.Automatic Transmiision or Manual<P> 2. 6 cylinder or 4<P> 3. When was the last major tune up<P>  from here we would check to see if fuel pressure is correct as to it might be your fuel pump going out - possibilty also that the timing might be off<P> I will asume that sensors are correct and functional seeing as how you said you past smog - start off by answering these questions and we'll find the problem<P><BR>Eric - West Coast Fiero <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> <BR>310-305-4111||||reg||1
